<p>A <strong>backfill</strong> supplies new values for existing records. A reliable backfill also explains which records it covered, what happened to each one and where to resume after interruption. That matters when the database is still serving requests: yesterday’s source value may be out of date before the worker tries to store its result.</p>
<p>The shop is replacing free-text delivery addresses with structured fields. Mina can edit an order while the job runs, and some addresses need human confirmation. We will follow one job from its input contract to its completion evidence. The <a href="/review/relational-next/live-changes/#keep-old-and-new-applications-compatible">parent’s bridge release</a> is a prerequisite: every writer, including delayed jobs, must maintain the agreed representation protocol before trusted conversion starts.</p>
<p>The figures are illustrative schedules. A downloadable rehearsal checks the concrete procedures on native PostgreSQL 18; our run used 18.6. Its small invented address grammar tests job behaviour, rather than providing a production address parser.</p>

